# TypeORM & PostgreSQL

- `synchronize` is always `false`. Schema changes go through migrations
- UUID primary keys. Timestamps as `timestamptz`
- Soft delete only on `Activity` (`DeleteDateColumn`). Users and students use hard delete + `ON DELETE RESTRICT`
- Unique activity: `(student_id, activity_date, activity_type)` WHERE `deleted_at IS NULL`
- Child rows (`activity_items`, `activity_materials`): `ON DELETE CASCADE`
- Behavior reports and notes: `ON DELETE RESTRICT` (independent documents)
- Companion FK must be a `User` with role `PENDAMPING` (enforced in service layer)
- Multi-table writes (create/update activity + children) must use a transaction
- Name indexes/FKs explicitly (`IDX_`, `UQ_`, `FK_`, `CHK_`)
- Login identifier is `email` (unique, stored lowercase), not username

```typescript
// BAD
synchronize: true

// GOOD
synchronize: false
migrations: ['dist/database/migrations/*.js']
```
